<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sadaqa ibn Mansur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1108</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sadaqa ibn Mansur was the most powerful ruler of the Mazyadid dynasty of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, an Arab Shia family. Around 1101 he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hilla">al-Hilla</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> near ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, which became the capital of the dynasty and a great centre of Shia learning. He was killed in 1108 fighting the Seljuk sultan Muhammad I.</p></div>
